    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (69.14) and **James Wood** (69.03) anchoring our offensive production. **James Wood** is particularly well-positioned as he leads off against Taj Bradley, benefiting from an elite lineup spot multiplier (+10%) and a favorable xERA of 4.27. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** provides our highest ceiling; while he faces Bubba Chandler, his dynamic platoon advantage and projected speed profile make him a core building block. We are also leaning heavily on the top-of-the-order power of **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.53) and **Brice Turang** (68.46). **Brice Turang** remains a focal point for our stolen base strategy, as his matchup against Andre Pallante features a slow pitcher delivery profile that boosts his efficiency score by 4%. \n\nWe are navigating a few high-risk matchups, most notably **Jose Caballero** (41.62), whose score is suppressed by a brutal draw against Jacob deGrom. His low score is a direct result of a significant SP skill penalty (-19%) and a poor order placement (-8%). Among our bench decisions, **Cole Young** (42.34) was the closest to cracking the starting lineup. While he projects as a marginal play, he was ultimately bypassed due to his lower base projection and a unfavorable park adjustment, which prevented him from eclipsing the efficiency of our back-end outfielders. **Mickey Moniak** is removed from all consideration due to a confirmed rainout, while **Luis Campusano** continues to be excluded due to a difficult matchup against Logan Webb. Users should monitor the pending status of our entire lineup, as any late-breaking changes to batting order spots for **Gabriel Moreno** or **Dalton Rushing** will necessitate immediate recalibration of their sub-50 efficiency scores.",
